# syntek-base only — this file is copier-excluded, so a generated project never receives it.
#
# Handoffs written while developing the TEMPLATE are session state, not template content:
# they name in-flight work on syntek-base itself and are pruned once that work resumes.
# A generated project's handoffs are its own and stay tracked, which is what
# handoffs/CONTEXT.md describes.
#
# The CONTEXT.md / CLAUDE.md pair stays tracked so the folder ships documented.
HANDOFF-*.md
